 occurs when the parseProxyProtocolV1 method processes multiple requests on the same HTTP connection. As a result, different requests may share the same StringBuilder instance, potentially leading to information leakage between requests or responses. In some cases, a value from a previous request or response may be erroneously reused, which could lead to unintended data exposure. This issue primarily results in errors and connection termination but creates a risk of data leakage in multi-request environments.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Undertow: improper state management in proxy protocol parsing causes information leakage","topics":["advisory","cwe-362"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-27T08:45:20.072931Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2024-3653"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-27T09:39:10.911967Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-27T09:39:10.911967Z","id":"osv:CVE-2024-3653","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2024-07-08T21:21:20.899000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","https://access.redhat.com/jbossnetwork/restricted/listSoftware.html","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:4392","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:5143","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:5144","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:5145","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:5147","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:6437","https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2024-3653","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2024/3xxx/CVE-2024-3653.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-3653","https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20240828-0002/","https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2274437","https://github.com/undertow-io/undertow"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":[],"patch_status":"unknown","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2024-3653","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2024-3653"},"summary":"A vulnerability was found in Undertow. This issue requires enabling the learning-push handler in the server's config, which is disabled by default, leaving the maxAge config in the handler unconfigured. The default is -1, which makes the handler vulnerable. If someone overwrites that config, the server is not subject to the attack. The attacker needs to be able to reach the server with a normal HTTP request.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Undertow: learningpushhandler can lead to remote memory dos attacks","topics":["advisory","cwe-401"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-27T08:45:46.849545Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2024-5971"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-27T09:39:10.911967Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-27T09:39:10.911967Z","id":"osv:CVE-2024-5971","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2024-07-08T20:51:29.223000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","https://access.redhat.com/jbossnetwork/restricted/listSoftware.html","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:4392","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:4884","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:5143","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:5144","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:5145","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:5147","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:6508","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:6883","https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2024-5971","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2024/5xxx/CVE-2024-5971.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-5971","https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20240828-0001/","https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2292211","https://github.com/undertow-io/undertow"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2024-5971"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2024-5971","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2024-5971"},"summary":"A vulnerability was found in Undertow, where the chunked response hangs after the body was flushed. The response headers and body were sent but the client would continue waiting as Undertow does not send the expected 0\\r\\n termination of the chunked response. This results in uncontrolled resource consumption, leaving the server side to a denial of service attack. This happens only with Java 17 TLSv1.3 scenarios.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Undertow: response write hangs in case of java 17 tlsv1.3 newsessionticket","topics":["advisory","cwe-674"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-26T18:45:17.427850Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2024-1635"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-27T09:39:10.911967Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-27T09:39:10.911967Z","id":"osv:CVE-2024-1635","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2024-02-19T21:23:14.496000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","https://access.redhat.com/jbossnetwork/restricted/listSoftware.html","https://catalog.redhat.com/software/containers/","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1674","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1675","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1676","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1677","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1860","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1861","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1862","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1864","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1866","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:3354","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:4884","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2025:4226","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2025:9583","https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2024-1635","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2024/1xxx/CVE-2024-1635.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-1635","https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20240322-0007/"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":[],"patch_status":"unknown","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2024-1635","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2024-1635"},"summary":"A vulnerability was found in Undertow. This vulnerability impacts a server that supports the wildfly-http-client protocol. Whenever a malicious user opens and closes a connection with the HTTP port of the server and then closes the connection immediately, the server will end with both memory and open file limits exhausted at some point, depending on the amount of memory available. \r\n\r\nAt HTTP upgrade to remoting, the WriteTimeoutStreamSinkConduit leaks connections if RemotingConnection is closed by Remoting ServerConnectionOpenListener. Because the remoting connection originates in Undertow as part of the HTTP upgrade, there is an external layer to the remoting connection. This connection is unaware of the outermost layer when closing the connection during the connection opening procedure. Hence, the Undertow WriteTimeoutStreamSinkConduit is not notified of the closed connection in this scenario. Because WriteTimeoutStreamSinkConduit creates a timeout task, the whole dependency tree leaks via that task, which is added to XNIO WorkerThread. So, the workerThread points to the Undertow conduit, which contains the connections and causes the leak.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Undertow: out-of-memory error after several closed connections with wildfly-http-client protocol","topics":["advisory","cwe-400"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-27T08:45:43.039133Z","vendors":[]}],"meta":{"cve_inputs":["CVE-2026-80456","CVE-2026-80455","CVE-2026-80454","CVE-2026-80453","CVE-2026-80452","CVE-2026-80451","CVE-2026-80450","CVE-2026-80449","CVE-2026-80448","CVE-2026-80447","CVE-2026-80268","CVE-2026-80248","CVE-2026-80246","CVE-2026-80245","CVE-2026-80244","CVE-2026-59103","CVE-2026-137609","CVE-2026-133941","CVE-2026-133940","CVE-2026-133939","CVE-2026-133938","CVE-2026-133845","CVE-2026-133842","CVE-2026-132890","CVE-2026-122093","CVE-2026-115841","CVE-2026-115836","CVE-2026-115835","CVE-2026-115834","CVE-2026-95622","CVE-2026-80243","CVE-2026-110928","CVE-2025-70034","CVE-2025-41671","CVE-2025-25272","CVE-2024-7885","CVE-2024-5971","CVE-2024-3884","CVE-2024-3653","CVE-2024-1635"],"errors":[],"fetched_at":"2026-11-27T09:39:10.911967+00:00","normalized_count":5,"not_found_count":35,"osv_id_count":5,"query_count":40,"raw_count":5,"source":"OSV.dev /v1/vulns","status":"success"}}
